WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.765
Before and after twenty fifteen.

00:00:02.715 --> 00:00:05.272
A decade of documented decline.

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:12.568
This page presents side-by-side comparisons of Canada in twenty fifteen versus twenty twenty-five across twelve key metrics.

00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:16.090
MAID deaths: zero to seventy-six thousand.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.386
Federal debt: six hundred twelve billion to one point two trillion.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:24.318
Housing ratio: five times income to eight times.

00:00:24.318 --> 00:00:28.874
Military CDS changes: zero to three in three years.

00:00:28.874 --> 00:00:31.795
Every number comes from official government data.

00:00:31.795 --> 00:00:34.579
The decade of decline is not alleged.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:37.977
It is documented in the government's own statistics.

00:00:37.977 --> 00:00:40.920
The question is not whether Canada declined.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.102
The question is whether the decline was accidental or architectural.

00:00:45.102 --> 00:00:47.136
The comparison table.

00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:51.102
Twelve metrics comparing twenty fifteen to twenty twenty five.

00:00:51.102 --> 00:00:53.045
The pattern of decline.

00:00:53.045 --> 00:00:57.761
Eleven of twelve metrics worsened or failed to improve meaningfully over the decade.

00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:04.931
The one improvement — boil water advisories — cost eight point two billion dollars and still has twenty-eight advisories remaining.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.499
MAID went from zero to seventy-six thousand deaths.

00:01:08.499 --> 00:01:10.340
Federal debt doubled.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.715
Housing became unaffordable.

00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:15.272
The military leadership collapsed.

00:01:15.272 --> 00:01:18.511
Ethics violations had zero consequences.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:24.522
GDP per capita declined while total GDP grew on immigration-driven population increase.

00:01:24.522 --> 00:01:30.954
The corporate tax rate remained unchanged at fifteen percent while every metric of public service deteriorated.

00:01:30.954 --> 00:01:40.102
The question the data asks: if every metric worsens over a decade while one political party governs for nine of those ten years, is the decline accidental or architectural?

00:01:40.102 --> 00:01:44.386
The system architecture documented across this site provides the answer.
